## 🧪 Retrofit `enqueue()` vs `execute()`

| Feature      | `enqueue()` (Async)                 | `execute()` (Sync)             |
| ------------ | ----------------------------------- | ------------------------------ |
| Thread       | Background                          | Current (Blocking)             |
| Main Thread? | ✅ Safe                              | ❌ Not safe                     |
| Callback     | Yes (onResponse/onFailure)          | No (direct response/exception) |
| Use Case     | UI interactions, ViewModel API call | WorkManager, background jobs   |

**Best:** Use `suspend` with Coroutines

```kotlin
@GET("users/{id}")
suspend fun getUser(@Path("id") id: Int): User
```

